## Precedence (single source — do not duplicate elsewhere)

1. Explicit current user instruction, **including requested output schema**
2. Security / secrets / data-safety / git hard guardrails
3. Accepted architecture & product invariants
4. Task-specific rule matching the task (kids / model-routing globs)
5. Default execution & response-format policy (alwaysApply FORMAT + GitHub rules)
6. Human docs & current implementation state

Explicit user schema **overrides** FORMAT A/B/C, but **cannot** omit honest disclosure of: task status, validation, changed files, commit/push state, blockers/errors, and Codex result when Codex is required.

Code divergence ≠ product canon.

