## Status field names (do not collapse into one “Verdict”)

| Field | Values |
|-------|--------|
| **Task status** | `done` \| `partial` \| `blocked` \| `failed` \| `read-only` |
| **Codex commit gate** / **Codex review verdict** | `safe_to_commit` \| `needs_fixes` \| `unsafe_scope` (or user-requested domain trio e.g. `safe_to_adopt` / `needs_rules_fixes` / `unsafe_or_conflicting`) |
| **Codex reviewer status** | `approve` \| `approve-with-notes` \| `request-changes` \| `not run` \| `pending` |

`pending` = Codex is the required next step and has not started yet; executor must not claim commit-ready. Do not mix with Task status or gate verdict.

Mapping example: `safe_to_commit` ≈ `approve`/`approve-with-notes`; `needs_fixes`/`unsafe_scope` ≈ `request-changes`.

If Codex is **required** but not run → Task status cannot be commit-ready `done` → use `partial` or `blocked` (reviewer status `pending` or `not run` as appropriate).

